I'll use a frequency map then bucket by count: buckets[i] holds elements appearing i times. That's O(n) time and O(n) space. Edge cases: k larger than unique count returns everything; ties broken arbitrarily which I'll state. Alternative is a heap at O(n log k) — worse here. Let me write it: def top_k(nums, k): from collections import Counter; c = Counter(nums); buckets: list[list[int]] = [[] for _ in range(len(nums)+1)];
for num, freq in c.items(): buckets[freq].append(num);
res = [];
for i in range(len(buckets)-1, 0, -1):
 for num in buckets[i]:
  res.append(num);
  if len(res) == k: return res;
return res
